Java 17 (released September 2021) is an LTS (Long-Term Support) release. Besides its own new JEPs, most developers upgrade from Java 8 or 11 to gain all intermediate modern language features (records, text blocks, switch expressions, pattern matching, sealed types, etc.).
Below I’ll first list key features that became final or new in Java 17 itself, then a “since-last-LTS (11 → 17)” recap so you see what you newly gain overall. Each has simple examples.

✅ A. New / Finalized / Important in Java 17 Release
Area	JEP / Status	What It Gives You	Quick Note
Sealed Classes	JEP 409 (final)	Restrict which classes/interfaces can extend or implement a type	Better controlled inheritance & exhaustive pattern handling
Pattern Matching for switch	JEP 406 (Preview in 17)	Use patterns (type + conditions) in switch labels	Preview: requires --enable-preview
Enhanced Pseudo-Random Number Generators	JEP 356	New RNG hierarchy + jumpable/splittable algorithms	Better performance & reproducibility
Strong Encapsulation of JDK Internals	JEP 403	sun.* internals no longer accessible by default	Forces use of supported APIs
Deprecate Security Manager for Removal	JEP 411	Security Manager now legacy	Prepare to remove in future
Foreign Function & Memory API (Incubator 2)	JEP 412	Safer, performant interop with native code (C libs, off-heap memory)	Incubating; replace JNI in future
Context-Specific Deserialization Filters	JEP 415	Per-stream filters to curb deserialization gadget attacks	Security hardening
macOS/AArch64 Port	JEP 391	Native support on Apple Silicon	Performance & battery gains
Applet API Deprecated for Removal	JEP 398	Applets effectively end-of-life	Legacy cleanup

Note: “Preview” means you must compile & run with --enable-preview --release 17 (or --source 17) to use that feature in preview form. “Incubator” modules need --add-modules.

1. Sealed Classes & Interfaces (Final)
Control inheritance: only permitted types can extend/implement.


public sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Rectangle, Square { }

public final class Circle implements Shape {
    double radius;
    public Circle(double r) { this.radius = r; }
}

public non-sealed class Rectangle implements Shape {
    double w, h;
    public Rectangle(double w, double h) { this.w = w; this.h = h; }
}

public final class Square extends Rectangle {
    public Square(double side) { super(side, side); }
}
When to use:

Define a closed hierarchy (better than enums when variants carry distinct data).

Enables more exhaustive pattern handling (with switch pattern matching preview).

2. Pattern Matching for switch (Preview in 17)
Add type patterns, guarded patterns, null handling in switch.


static String describe(Object o) {
    return switch (o) {
        case null -> "null";
        case String s && s.isBlank() -> "Blank string";
        case String s -> "String of length " + s.length();
        case Circle c -> "Circle radius=" + c.radius;
        case Rectangle r && r.w == r.h -> "A square-ish rectangle";
        default -> "Something else";
    };
}
